1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:10,467
<i> [LIVELY MUSIC]</i>

2
00:00:12,633 --> 00:00:15,333
<i>Previously on You're My Favorite
Song...</i>

3
00:00:17,233 --> 00:00:18,933
<i>Are you sure about this, Miguel?</i>

4
00:00:19,067 --> 00:00:20,967
<i>You're going to busk in public?</i>

5
00:00:21,100 --> 00:00:22,400
<i>What if someone recognizes you?</i>

6
00:00:22,533 --> 00:00:23,733
<i> Don't worry, Bro.</i>

7
00:00:23,867 --> 00:00:25,067
<i> No one will recognize me.</i>

8
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:27,967
<i>I just want to sing again
without being mobbed.</i>

9
00:00:28,100 --> 00:00:35,467
<i> [SOFT MUSIC]</i>

10
00:00:35,633 --> 00:00:37,933
<i>Oh no, the curry spilled
in my bag!</i>

11
00:00:41,867 --> 00:00:43,233
<i> Sorry, I'm sorry.</i>

12
00:00:43,367 --> 00:00:45,267
<i> Hey, get back here!</i>

13
00:00:45,400 --> 00:00:48,367
<i>Finally, I found you,
you troublemaking teddy bear.</i>

14
00:00:48,500 --> 00:00:50,567
<i>You're the one who spilled
chicken curry on my bag.</i>

15
00:00:50,700 --> 00:00:53,000
<i>I'm sorry I ran off
after I stained your bag.</i>

16
00:00:53,133 --> 00:00:54,133
<i> I got you a new one.</i>

17
00:00:54,267 --> 00:00:55,000
<i> Friends?</i>

18
00:00:55,133 --> 00:00:56,400
<i> Fine.</i>

19
00:00:56,533 --> 00:00:57,700
<i> Friends.</i>

20
00:00:57,833 --> 00:01:01,300
<i>Every Friday,
he sings at Manila Park.</i>

21
00:01:01,433 --> 00:01:03,800
<i>He never told me
who he really was.</i>

22
00:01:03,933 --> 00:01:05,267
<i> He said it was a secret.</i>

23
00:01:05,400 --> 00:01:07,800
<i> So I gave him a nickname.</i>

24
00:01:07,967 --> 00:01:09,667
<i> "Captain Serenade,"</i>

25
00:01:09,800 --> 00:01:11,600
<i>because of his captain-style
cap.</i>

26
00:01:12,700 --> 00:01:14,133
<i> But one day...</i>

27
00:01:15,300 --> 00:01:16,967
<i>we suddenly stopped seeing
each other.</i>

28
00:01:18,600 --> 00:01:22,767
<i>My grandfather was diagnosed
with stage 3 pancreatic cancer.</i>

29
00:01:24,200 --> 00:01:25,467
<i> So even though it hurt,</i>

30
00:01:26,500 --> 00:01:29,400
<i>Grandfather Xavi and I went
through his bucket list.</i>

31
00:01:29,533 --> 00:01:30,667
<i> Are you ready for...</i>

32
00:01:30,800 --> 00:01:34,133
<i>It's a list of things he wants
to do before he's gone.</i>

33
00:01:34,267 --> 00:01:35,267
<i>- Ready.
- Okay.</i>

34
00:01:35,400 --> 00:01:37,800
<i>Number one, this is the most
important.</i>

35
00:01:39,567 --> 00:01:41,800
<i> "To build..."</i>

36
00:01:41,967 --> 00:01:43,100
<i> Yes.</i>

37
00:01:44,333 --> 00:01:46,900
<i>When your grandmother
and I got this property,</i>

38
00:01:47,033 --> 00:01:49,133
<i> we never let it go.</i>

39
00:01:49,267 --> 00:01:51,833
<i>Will your remaining retirement
pay be enough</i>

40
00:01:51,967 --> 00:01:53,933
<i>along with what little
I've saved from selling turon</i>

41
00:01:54,067 --> 00:01:55,667
<i> to build our resort?</i>

42
00:01:55,800 --> 00:01:58,600
<i>The resorts we saw were all
so beautiful,</i>

43
00:01:58,733 --> 00:02:00,300
<i> especially that Monta...</i>

44
00:02:00,433 --> 00:02:02,500
<i> Montaverde Group of Hotels.</i>

45
00:02:02,633 --> 00:02:04,300
<i> We can do this, Mama Bebe.</i>

46
00:02:04,433 --> 00:02:07,367
<i>- Group hug!
- Group hug!</i>

47
00:02:07,500 --> 00:02:10,233
<i>The next three months weren't
easy.</i>

48
00:02:10,367 --> 00:02:14,300
<i>We did everything to finish
the resort.</i>

49
00:02:14,467 --> 00:02:18,967
<i>We poured everything
we had into it.</i>

50
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:29,933
["YOU'RE MY FAVORITE SONG"
BY PRINCESS ALIYAH]

51
00:03:13,133 --> 00:03:14,233
What's that, Angel?

52
00:03:14,367 --> 00:03:15,167
Let me help you.

53
00:03:15,300 --> 00:03:16,767
- Okay.
- What do you need to do?

54
00:03:16,900 --> 00:03:18,600
Let's just do it here,
Grandfather Xavi.

55
00:03:18,733 --> 00:03:20,633
Ah, you want to make it
permanent?

56
00:03:20,800 --> 00:03:23,133
- Yes.
- Hold on.

57
00:03:23,267 --> 00:03:25,033
Thank you.

58
00:03:25,167 --> 00:03:26,667
- All right, snack time first.
- It looks a bit too short.

59
00:03:26,800 --> 00:03:28,700
Grab some turon first, hurry.

60
00:03:28,833 --> 00:03:31,500
- It still seems short.
- So we can have our snack.

61
00:03:31,633 --> 00:03:33,133
- Okay. All right.
- I'll find a bigger nail.

62
00:03:33,267 --> 00:03:34,800
- Okay, Grandfather Xavi.
- Okay.

63
00:03:34,933 --> 00:03:37,667
Dad, Angel,
let's have a snack first.

64
00:03:39,867 --> 00:03:41,233
Thank you, Mama Bebe.

65
00:03:41,367 --> 00:03:44,467
Okay.

66
00:03:44,600 --> 00:03:45,500
Oh my.

67
00:03:45,633 --> 00:03:46,933
What's that? Is that the one
with leche flan?

68
00:03:47,067 --> 00:03:48,767
Oh, yes.

69
00:03:48,900 --> 00:03:50,567
Let me fix this first, Dad.

70
00:03:52,567 --> 00:03:54,867
Grandfather Xavi,
when we were moving,

71
00:03:55,033 --> 00:03:58,167
I found this tucked inside
a book.

72
00:03:58,300 --> 00:04:00,767
This is Mama Bebe, right?

73
00:04:00,900 --> 00:04:02,200
Who's the other woman?

74
00:04:08,267 --> 00:04:10,533
So there are still memories
of Serina left.

75
00:04:14,067 --> 00:04:17,033
I thought everything was burned
in our old house.

76
00:04:19,167 --> 00:04:20,233
Serina?

77
00:04:22,967 --> 00:04:25,600
She's your Mama Bebe's
younger sister.

78
00:04:27,300 --> 00:04:28,700
But...

79
00:04:28,867 --> 00:04:31,900
that was more than 17 years
ago...

80
00:04:33,867 --> 00:04:35,567
when she left home.

81
00:04:35,700 --> 00:04:38,300
We had a falling out.

82
00:04:38,833 --> 00:04:41,100
And until now...

83
00:04:41,233 --> 00:04:43,133
we're still looking for her.

84
00:04:45,333 --> 00:04:46,633
Maybe we should have,
Grandfather Xavi,

85
00:04:46,767 --> 00:04:49,067
added this to your bucket list.

86
00:04:49,200 --> 00:04:53,100
To find Aunt Serina and make
things right between you.

87
00:04:53,233 --> 00:04:57,333
Child, it's hard to find someone
who doesn't want to be found.

88
00:05:00,500 --> 00:05:03,800
Your grandfather and I don't
talk about Serina

89
00:05:03,967 --> 00:05:08,900
because he cries every time
my sister comes up.

90
00:05:09,033 --> 00:05:11,267
She carried a lot of anger
toward us back then.

91
00:05:11,400 --> 00:05:13,600
But honestly...

92
00:05:13,733 --> 00:05:17,000
she's the one responsible
for how her life turned out.

93
00:05:18,533 --> 00:05:20,333
Beverly, that's enough.

94
00:05:21,633 --> 00:05:24,000
All right, let's put this away
for now.

95
00:05:24,133 --> 00:05:25,133
Okay.

96
00:05:25,267 --> 00:05:28,233
By the way...

97
00:05:28,367 --> 00:05:29,667
I wanted to ask,

98
00:05:29,800 --> 00:05:34,533
why did you choose the name
"Gran Vista" for the resort?

99
00:05:34,700 --> 00:05:35,733
Well, Grandfather Xavi,

100
00:05:35,867 --> 00:05:39,467
we have the best sunset here
in Solmera,

101
00:05:39,600 --> 00:05:43,967
so "Gran Vista" in Spanish means
"best view."

102
00:05:45,867 --> 00:05:47,033
Spanish.

103
00:05:47,167 --> 00:05:48,800
Looks like she knows a thing
or two.

104
00:05:48,933 --> 00:05:49,933
Makes sense, right?

105
00:05:50,067 --> 00:05:53,233
You know, the view is beautiful,
but it feels like...

106
00:05:53,367 --> 00:05:55,767
it's kind of being blocked
by this signage.

107
00:05:56,900 --> 00:05:57,933
We need to move it.

108
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:01,000
Shift it back...

109
00:06:01,133 --> 00:06:02,800
Guys, give me a hand here.

110
00:06:04,900 --> 00:06:05,900
[XAVI GROANS]

111
00:06:06,033 --> 00:06:07,767
Dad!

112
00:06:07,933 --> 00:06:09,033
Are you okay?

113
00:06:09,167 --> 00:06:10,167
Dad.

114
00:06:11,500 --> 00:06:13,000
Dad.

115
00:06:13,133 --> 00:06:14,467
I'm fine, I'm fine.

116
00:06:15,933 --> 00:06:16,933
It just went down the wrong way.

117
00:06:18,533 --> 00:06:20,733
- Come on, Dad.
- Let them handle it.

118
00:06:20,867 --> 00:06:22,733
Just move it a bit
so we can see the sunset.

119
00:06:22,867 --> 00:06:25,033
All right, you take care of it.

120
00:06:25,167 --> 00:06:26,333
I'm okay.

121
00:06:27,500 --> 00:06:29,633
Come on, let's eat our snack.

122
00:06:31,733 --> 00:06:33,300
- Please sit down first.
- Dad, sit down first.

123
00:06:33,433 --> 00:06:35,100
I'll just bring it to you.

124
00:06:37,900 --> 00:06:39,033
I'm fine.

125
00:06:39,267 --> 00:06:40,733
Don't carry anything for now...

126
00:06:42,867 --> 00:06:44,267
no lifting.

127
00:06:49,800 --> 00:06:50,967
Gran Vista.

128
00:06:52,000 --> 00:06:53,267
That's Spanish.

129
00:06:54,800 --> 00:06:56,067
Oh, is that yours?

130
00:06:56,200 --> 00:06:58,267
- This one.
- This one.

131
00:06:58,400 --> 00:07:08,367
[GENTLE MUSIC]

132
00:07:10,733 --> 00:07:19,267
[BRIGHT MUSIC]

133
00:07:19,433 --> 00:07:21,100
Wow, it looks so beautiful now.

134
00:07:21,233 --> 00:07:23,900
- It's probably almost done.
- Thank you.

135
00:07:24,033 --> 00:07:25,700
When will that open?

136
00:07:36,300 --> 00:07:39,567
My child,
we've finished the resort.

137
00:07:39,700 --> 00:07:42,067
We're deep in debt and we spent
everything we had,

138
00:07:42,200 --> 00:07:44,033
but we finished it.

139
00:07:44,167 --> 00:07:46,000
We can finally have our grand
opening!

140
00:07:47,967 --> 00:07:51,100
But Angel, my dear,
just remember this,

141
00:07:51,233 --> 00:07:54,800
even when the resort is running
and earning,

142
00:07:54,933 --> 00:07:57,200
never ever neglect your studies.

143
00:07:58,267 --> 00:07:59,733
You know, it's still
on my bucket list

144
00:07:59,867 --> 00:08:02,967
to place a medal on you
when you graduate senior high.

145
00:08:04,533 --> 00:08:06,567
Grandfather Xavi,
even in college, okay?

146
00:08:06,700 --> 00:08:10,200
You and Mama Bebe should be
the ones to give me my medal.

147
00:08:11,733 --> 00:08:12,600
All the way to college?

148
00:08:12,733 --> 00:08:13,833
Yes.

149
00:08:16,333 --> 00:08:17,900
Dad.

150
00:08:18,033 --> 00:08:19,200
You'll make it that far.

151
00:08:22,233 --> 00:08:24,167
That's still far away.

152
00:08:24,400 --> 00:08:27,533
But Grandfather Xavi,
promise me this.

153
00:08:28,800 --> 00:08:32,933
Once the resort starts earning,
you'll go through chemotherapy.

154
00:08:41,567 --> 00:08:42,867
All right, I will.

155
00:08:43,000 --> 00:08:44,000
I promise.

156
00:08:44,133 --> 00:08:46,433
Promise, okay, Grandfather.

157
00:08:51,000 --> 00:08:52,100
So, my child, what now?

158
00:08:52,233 --> 00:08:52,833
What?

159
00:08:52,967 --> 00:08:55,200
- Group hug.
- Group hug?

160
00:08:55,367 --> 00:08:56,833
Group hug!

161
00:08:56,967 --> 00:09:00,100
- Group hug, group hug.
- Yes, this is exciting.

162
00:09:07,167 --> 00:09:17,133
[SOFT TENSE MUSIC]

163
00:09:32,800 --> 00:09:36,233
I won't allow your resort
to succeed.

164
00:09:37,367 --> 00:09:39,167
You've done so much wrong to me.

165
00:09:40,700 --> 00:09:44,267
And I will make sure...

166
00:09:44,400 --> 00:09:46,600
your family falls.

167
00:09:48,033 --> 00:09:50,533
And your resort...

168
00:09:50,667 --> 00:09:54,667
will soon be part
of the Montaverde empire.

169
00:10:30,367 --> 00:10:40,333
[LIVELY MUSIC]

170
00:10:59,500 --> 00:11:01,700
What remained of Grandfather
Xavi's savings was spent here

171
00:11:01,833 --> 00:11:04,867
at Brighton Bay Academy...

172
00:11:07,133 --> 00:11:10,467
the most prestigious school
in Solmera City.

173
00:11:11,533 --> 00:11:21,467
["YOU'RE MY FAVORITE SONG"
BY PRINCESS ALIYAH]

174
00:12:01,967 --> 00:12:04,300
<i>Oh no, the curry spilled
in my bag.</i>

175
00:12:04,433 --> 00:12:06,633
<i> Here, I got you a new one.</i>

176
00:12:10,167 --> 00:12:11,133
<i> Do you approve?</i>

177
00:12:18,533 --> 00:12:21,233
<i>Sometimes, I still think
about Captain Serenade.</i>

178
00:12:22,367 --> 00:12:26,767
<i>Did he get mad at me
for suddenly disappearing?</i>

179
00:12:29,367 --> 00:12:31,767
<i>Is he still busking
at Manila Park?</i>

180
00:12:33,433 --> 00:12:36,300
<i>Has he written a lot
of new songs by now?</i>

181
00:12:36,433 --> 00:12:37,767
the girl...

182
00:12:40,200 --> 00:12:44,100
Who prayed for me in silence...

183
00:12:45,400 --> 00:12:48,933
with simple dreams.

184
00:12:49,100 --> 00:12:53,367
And deep kindness in your hands.

185
00:12:53,500 --> 00:12:55,700
Ouch.

186
00:12:55,833 --> 00:12:58,067
What the hell?
Can you let me go already?

187
00:12:58,200 --> 00:12:59,033
Let go? Get up.

188
00:12:59,167 --> 00:13:00,700
That hurts!

189
00:13:00,833 --> 00:13:02,967
Why am I always your favorite
punching bag?

190
00:13:03,100 --> 00:13:04,933
- What?
- Let me go already.

191
00:13:05,067 --> 00:13:06,567
- Bro.
- Tie him up.

192
00:13:06,700 --> 00:13:08,533
Give him to me.

193
00:13:08,667 --> 00:13:10,367
- His hands.
- Punching bag?

194
00:13:10,500 --> 00:13:12,467
You're such an idiot, Zion.

195
00:13:12,600 --> 00:13:14,233
I'm not beating you up.

196
00:13:14,367 --> 00:13:16,733
I just need some scratch paper.

197
00:13:18,000 --> 00:13:19,033
Hey, man.

198
00:13:21,900 --> 00:13:23,167
Not on your head.

199
00:13:25,067 --> 00:13:26,933
- Write on him, Bro.
- It's already crumpled.

200
00:13:27,067 --> 00:13:28,600
Write on him, Calix.

201
00:13:28,733 --> 00:13:30,267
There.

202
00:13:30,400 --> 00:13:31,933
Keep going.

203
00:13:33,300 --> 00:13:34,667
- Scratch paper.
- There.

204
00:13:34,800 --> 00:13:36,767
- What equation is that?
- Thank you for...

205
00:13:36,900 --> 00:13:38,467
being a sacrifice.

206
00:13:40,500 --> 00:13:41,433
There, write on that.

207
00:13:41,567 --> 00:13:42,533
Go on.

208
00:13:44,033 --> 00:13:45,833
Calix, please.

209
00:13:45,967 --> 00:13:48,033
The bell's about to ring,
Ma'am is coming.

210
00:13:48,167 --> 00:13:49,800
- Scratch paper.
- Yo, Calix.

211
00:13:49,933 --> 00:13:52,000
What if we write on his glasses
instead?

212
00:13:52,133 --> 00:13:53,933
- Yes, Bro.
- Excuse me.

213
00:13:54,067 --> 00:13:55,433
- Excuse me!
- Let me see.

214
00:13:55,600 --> 00:13:56,700
Hey, what are you doing to him?

215
00:13:56,833 --> 00:13:57,900
Stop it.

216
00:14:00,700 --> 00:14:01,767
Who is this?

217
00:14:04,067 --> 00:14:05,400
And who the hell are you?

218
00:14:05,533 --> 00:14:12,367
[TENSE MUSIC]

219
00:14:13,000 --> 00:14:15,267
[LAUGHTER]

220
00:14:15,800 --> 00:14:17,567
- [CHUCKLING]
- Who is this?

221
00:14:19,067 --> 00:14:20,100
Are you lost?

222
00:14:24,367 --> 00:14:25,933
Oh, wait.

223
00:14:26,800 --> 00:14:27,833
Let me guess.

224
00:14:28,900 --> 00:14:30,767
You're the new junior high
transferee.

225
00:14:30,900 --> 00:14:32,967
- Ahh. That's her.
- Right?

226
00:14:33,100 --> 00:14:34,100
Oh.

227
00:14:34,500 --> 00:14:36,200
Yes, that's me.

228
00:14:36,933 --> 00:14:39,700
It's 2026, and bullying
is still the best

229
00:14:39,833 --> 00:14:41,267
your brain cells can do?

230
00:14:41,400 --> 00:14:43,167
- Of course.
- [PONCY LAUGHS]

231
00:14:48,833 --> 00:14:49,867
Let him go.

232
00:14:50,467 --> 00:14:51,767
- Let him go!
- Ow.

233
00:14:51,900 --> 00:14:53,067
Wow, how scary.

234
00:14:53,200 --> 00:14:54,267
And what if I don't?

235
00:14:56,833 --> 00:14:59,233
You think it's a flex
to humiliate someone?

236
00:15:00,800 --> 00:15:02,333
Why would I try to impress you?

237
00:15:03,867 --> 00:15:04,933
I know your type.

238
00:15:06,400 --> 00:15:08,233
- You're a weakling.
- Oh.

239
00:15:08,700 --> 00:15:10,267
Maybe you're the weakling.
Here's another one.

240
00:15:10,400 --> 00:15:13,200
You hurt others
just to look tough.

241
00:15:13,333 --> 00:15:15,900
But the truth is,
you're nothing.

242
00:15:16,033 --> 00:15:18,267
Hey, man, Calix.

243
00:15:18,400 --> 00:15:20,067
- She's got guts.
- You're bold.

244
00:15:20,200 --> 00:15:23,733
Yo, Miss Transferee,
for your information,

245
00:15:23,867 --> 00:15:25,900
Calix is the smartest student

246
00:15:26,033 --> 00:15:28,800
here at Brighton Bay Academy,
okay?

247
00:15:28,933 --> 00:15:31,467
No one can beat him
academically, okay?

248
00:15:31,600 --> 00:15:32,833
Know your place.

249
00:15:33,433 --> 00:15:34,400
As if.

250
00:15:35,600 --> 00:15:39,200
You have no idea
what I'm capable of here.

251
00:15:39,333 --> 00:15:40,967
[TENSE MUSIC]

252
00:15:41,100 --> 00:15:42,567
- Because I...
- She's about to cry.

253
00:15:44,167 --> 00:15:45,500
I'm the king here.

254
00:15:47,900 --> 00:15:49,400
Even the...

255
00:15:49,533 --> 00:15:51,567
the teachers,

256
00:15:51,700 --> 00:15:52,700
